[{"code":"top_level_list_changed","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":28,"col":8},"end":{"line":28,"col":19}},"title":"TOP-LEVEL LIST CHANGED","message":"`update` changes `model.done` and `model.open` in place, but when the program\nstarts each is `seed`, a top-level value.\n\n28|main = Tea.sandbox { init = λ⊤ → { done = seed, open = seed }, update = update, view = view }\n          ^^^^^^^^^^^ the runtime hands `update` the model here\n\n15|seed = [ 1 ]\n   ^^^^ the top-level list is defined here\n\nA top-level value is shared by every part of the program and never changes:\nchanged in place, it would change for every part that reads it.\n\nBuild the value inside `init ⊤`, so that each call makes fresh lists:\n\n    init ⊤ = …\n\nCall that function where the model is made. Wrapping `seed` in `λ⊤ → seed` still\nreturns the same shared value.\n\nThis is the language's rule for top-level values, whether or not anything else\nreads the list. `init` builds its model; a top-level value it returns is still\nshared (ownership-checker.md §22.2)."}]
